# ── Docker build context ignore ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this file the `COPY . .` in the build stage copies the HOST node_modules
# (macOS/arm64 native binaries for esbuild, sharp, @resvg, tailwind oxide, …) on
# top of the freshly-installed linux node_modules — producing an image whose
# native bindings are the wrong architecture ("container doesn't work as it
# should"). Ignoring node_modules (and the other noise below) keeps the build
# reproducible and small.

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image with --frozen-lockfile)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build / test output
dist
build
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.vite

# Secrets & local env (never bake into an image — injected by Coolify at runtime)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# VCS & tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Docs & planning (not needed to build the app)
docs
plans
*.md
!README.md

# Backups / scratch
package.json.bak
*.tgz
